   Transportation-BuildSys, Golden, CO, NOV 21-25, 2025},
Abstract = {Appliances and building systems consume a large portion of total energy.
   Detecting anomalies in their operation can reduce energy waste and
   maintenance costs. This Ph.D. work presents a TinyML-based edge learning
   framework for anomaly detection of appliance energy usage. Using a
   low-cost current sensor and STM32 microcontroller unit (MCU), root mean
   square (RMS) current and timestamped data will be collected from a
   mini-fridge. Lightweight models, optimized for on-device deployment, are
   planned. This work contributes to the BuildSys community by proposing a
   scalable, privacy-preserving approach for appliancelevel monitoring and
   early fault detection to improve energy efficiency.},
